{"id": "test_hand2-036", "split": "test_hand2", "intent": "no_tool", "family": -1, "request": "what is the difference between RAM and storage?", "expected": null, "reply": "RAM (Random Access Memory) and storage are two different components of a computer system, each with its own purpose and characteristics.\n\nRAM is a type of memory that stores data temporarily while the computer is running. It allows the computer to quickly access and manipulate data as it is needed, which is why it is often referred to as \"working\" memory. RAM is volatile, meaning that it loses all its contents when the power is turned off. It is used for storing programs, data, and other information that the computer needs to run efficiently.\n\nStorage, on the other hand, refers to the components of a computer system that store data permanently. This includes both internal storage (such as RAM) and external storage (such as hard drives, SSDs, and cloud storage). Storage allows the computer to store data for long periods of time, even when the power is off or the computer is turned off.\n\nIn summary, RAM is a type of memory that stores data temporarily while the computer is running, while storage is used to permanently store data.", "call": null, "verdict": null, "score": {"called": false, "levels": null, "abstained_ok": true, "error": null, "answered": null}}
